You can use `Promise.all()` to handle multiple API calls. This function waits for all promises to resolve and returns an array of results. Here's how you can use it:

```javascript
const apiCalls = [
  fetch('https://api.example.com/data1'),
  fetch('https://api.example.com/data2'),
  fetch('https://api.example.com/data3')
];

Promise.all(apiCalls)
  .then(results => {
    // results is an array containing the resolved values of all promises
    console.log(results);
  })
  .catch(error => {
    console.error('Error fetching data:', error);
  });
```

This approach ensures that all API calls are made and their results are available in the `results` array.
